This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Edit, Read</tools-used-before-summary>
Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   The user made two sequential requests:
   - Round 1: "Please review the current codebase and perform a general refactoring to improve its overall structure and quality."
   - Round 2: "Please continue with another round of general refactoring to further improve the codebase."
   Both requests are general refactoring passes over the SmartTube Android TV application codebase, aiming to improve structure, reduce duplication, and improve code quality without changing behavior.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Android TV app using Leanback library (BrowseFragment, PlaybackFragment, etc.)
   - ExoPlayer for video playback with custom glue classes
   - MVP architecture: Presenters, Views, Controllers
   - RxJava2 for async operations (Disposable, Observable)
   - Java backward-compatibility patterns for serialized data (`fromString`/`toString`)
   - Static factory methods (`Video.from(...)`, `VideoGroup.from(...)`)
   - WeakReference usage for memory management
   - Android's `TextUtils.isEmpty()` vs manual null + isEmpty checks
   - Lambda simplification (single-expression lambdas)
   - Early-return refactoring vs intermediate variables
   - Data-driven defaults arrays vs sequential if-blocks
   - Method extraction to eliminate duplicated logic
   - Overloaded helpers for adapter population (addButtonIfEnabled)
   - Auth-flag parameter to unify signed/unsigned dialog flows

3. Files and Code Sections:

   **Round 1 (committed in single commit "Refactor: simplify backward-compat loop, extract helpers, reduce duplication"):**

   - `common/src/main/java/com/liskovsoft/smartyoutubetv2/common/app/models/data/Video.java`
     - Most impactful file. Multiple improvements.
     - **`fromString()` backward compat**: Replaced 13 sequential `if (split.length == N)` blocks (50+ lines) with a compact while-loop using a static defaults array:
       ```java
       private static final String[] COMPAT_FIELD_DEFAULTS = {null, "-1", null, "-1", null, null, "-1", null, null, null, "false", "-1", null};
       private static final int COMPAT_FIELD_START = 10;
       // ...
       while (split.length >= COMPAT_FIELD_START && split.length < COMPAT_FIELD_START + COMPAT_FIELD_DEFAULTS.length) {
           split = Helpers.appendArray(split, new String[]{COMPAT_FIELD_DEFAULTS[split.length - COMPAT_FIELD_START]});
       }
       ```
     - **`sync(MediaItemFormatInfo)`**: Eliminated duplicate `formatInfo.isLive()` call:
       ```java
       isLive = formatInfo.isLive();
       if (isLive) {
           isUpcoming = false;
           startTimeMs = formatInfo.getStartTimeMs() > 0 ? formatInfo.getStartTimeMs() : DateHelper.toUnixTimeMs(formatInfo.getStartTimestamp());
           startSegmentNum = formatInfo.getStartSegmentNum();
       }
       ```
     - **`getChannelIdOrName()`**: Used `TextUtils.isEmpty()` for consistency:
       ```java
       public String getChannelIdOrName() {
           if (!TextUtils.isEmpty(channelId)) {
               return channelId;
           }
           String authorName = getAuthor();
           return !TextUtils.isEmpty(authorName) ? authorName : null;
       }
       ```
     - **`createPlaylistTitle()` / `createChannelTitle()`**: Replaced `String.format("%s", x)` with direct expressions:
       ```java
       return title != null && subtitle != null ? title + " - " + subtitle : title != null ? title : subtitle;
       ```

   - `common/src/main/java/com/liskovsoft/smartyoutubetv2/common/app/models/data/VideoGroup.java`
     - **`getType()`**: Flattened nested ternary to early-return form:
       ```java
       public int getType() {
           if (mType != -1) return mType;
           if (getMediaGroup() != null) return getMediaGroup().getType();
           return mSection != null ? mSection.getId() : -1;
       }
       ```
     - **`extractGroupPosition(Video)`**: Collapsed to single ternary:
       ```java
       private static int extractGroupPosition(Video item) {
           return item != null ? item.groupPosition : -1;
       }
       ```
     - **`findVideoById()`**: Eliminated intermediate variable with early return:
       ```java
       for (Video video : mVideos) {
           if (Helpers.equals(videoId, video.videoId)) {
               return video;
           }
       }
       return null;
       ```

   - `common/src/main/java/com/liskovsoft/smartyoutubetv2/common/app/presenters/BrowsePresenter.java`
     - **`shouldRememberSectionPosition()`**: Extracted duplicated condition:
       ```java
       private boolean shouldRememberSectionPosition() {
           return (isSubscriptionsSection() && getGeneralData().isRememberSubscriptionsPositionEnabled()) ||
                   (isPinnedSection() && getGeneralData().isRememberPinnedPositionEnabled());
       }
       ```
     - **`initPinnedData()`**: Merged `initPinnedSections()` + `initPinnedCallbacks()` (two separate iterations) into a single pass — both private methods removed:
       ```java
       private void initPinnedData() {
           mSections.clear();
           for (Video item : getSidebarService().getPinnedItems()) {
               if (item == null) {
                   continue;
               }
               if (item.sectionId == -1) { // pinned channel or playlist
                   mSections.add(createPinnedSection(item));
                   createPinnedMapping(item);
               } else {
                   BrowseSection section = mSectionsMapping.get(item.sectionId);
                   if (section != null) {
                       mSections.add(section);
                   }
               }
           }
           initPasswordSection();
       }
       ```
     - **`sortSections()`**: Simplified single-statement lambda:
       ```java
       Collections.sort(mSections,
               (o1, o2) -> getSidebarService().getSectionIndex(o1.getId()) - getSidebarService().getSectionIndex(o2.getId()));
       ```

   - `common/src/main/java/com/liskovsoft/smartyoutubetv2/common/misc/ScreensaverManager.java`
     - **`enable()`**: Cached `getScreensaverTimeoutMs()` to avoid double-call:
       ```java
       int timeoutMs = getGeneralData().getScreensaverTimeoutMs();
       int delayMs = timeoutMs == GeneralData.SCREENSAVER_TIMEOUT_NEVER ? 10_000 : timeoutMs;
       ```

   **Round 2 (NOT YET COMMITTED — changes exist in working tree):**

   - `smarttubetv/src/main/java/com/liskovsoft/smartyoutubetv2/tv/ui/playback/other/VideoPlayerGlue.java`
     - **`onCreatePrimaryActions()` and `onCreateSecondaryActions()`**: Extracted two overloaded helper methods to eliminate ~27 repetitive 3-line if-blocks. Before: each button was `if (mPlayerTweaksData.isPlayerButtonEnabled(X)) { adapter.add(mActions.get(Y)); }`. After:
       ```java
       private void addButtonIfEnabled(ArrayObjectAdapter adapter, int buttonId, int actionId) {
           if (mPlayerTweaksData.isPlayerButtonEnabled(buttonId)) {
               adapter.add(mActions.get(actionId));
           }
       }
       private void addButtonIfEnabled(ArrayObjectAdapter adapter, int buttonId, Action action) {
           if (mPlayerTweaksData.isPlayerButtonEnabled(buttonId)) {
               adapter.add(action);
           }
       }
       ```
     - Example usage in `onCreatePrimaryActions`:
       ```java
       addButtonIfEnabled(adapter, PlayerTweaksData.PLAYER_BUTTON_PREVIOUS, mSkipPreviousAction);
       addButtonIfEnabled(adapter, PlayerTweaksData.PLAYER_BUTTON_NEXT, mSkipNextAction);
       addButtonIfEnabled(adapter, PlayerTweaksData.PLAYER_BUTTON_REPEAT_MODE,    R.id.action_repeat);
       // ... etc.
       ```

   - `common/src/main/java/com/liskovsoft/smartyoutubetv2/common/app/models/playback/controllers/VideoStateController.java`
     - **`restoreVideoFormat()`**: Cached `getTempVideoFormat()` to avoid calling it twice:
       ```java
       private void restoreVideoFormat() {
           if (getPlayer() == null) {
               return;
           }
           FormatItem tempFormat = getPlayerData().getTempVideoFormat();
           getPlayer().setFormat(tempFormat != null ? tempFormat : getPlayerData().getFormat(FormatItem.TYPE_VIDEO));
       }
       ```

   - `common/src/main/java/com/liskovsoft/smartyoutubetv2/common/app/presenters/dialogs/menu/VideoMenuPresenter.java`
     - **Merged `prepareAndShowDialogSigned()` + `prepareAndShowDialogUnsigned()` into `prepareAndShowDialog(boolean isAuthenticated)`**:
       ```java
       private void prepareAndShowDialog(boolean isAuthenticated) {
           if (getContext() == null) {
               return;
           }
           appendReturnToBackgroundVideoButton();
           for (Long menuItem : MainUIData.instance(getContext()).getMenuItemsOrdered()) {
               MenuAction menuAction = mMenuMapping.get(menuItem);
               if (menuAction != null && (!menuAction.isAuth() || isAuthenticated)) {
                   menuAction.run();
               }
           }
           if (!mDialogPresenter.isEmpty()) {
               String title = mVideo != null ? mVideo.getTitle() : null;
               // No need to add author because: 1) This could be a channel card. 2) This info isn't so important.
               mDialogPresenter.showDialog(title);
           }
       }
       ```
     - `bootstrapPrepareAndShowDialogSigned` now calls `prepareAndShowDialog(true)`
     - `showMenu` lambda now calls `() -> prepareAndShowDialog(false)`

   - `common/src/main/java/com/liskovsoft/smartyoutubetv2/common/app/models/playback/controllers/SuggestionsController.java`
     - **`onControlsShown()` and `onSeekEnd()`**: Extracted duplicated branch into `updateChapterFocus(boolean)`:
       ```java
       @Override
       public void onControlsShown(boolean shown) {
           updateChapterFocus(shown);
       }
       @Override
       public void onSeekEnd() {
           if (getPlayer() == null) {
               return;
           }
           updateChapterFocus(getPlayer().isControlsShown());
       }
       private void updateChapterFocus(boolean controlsShown) {
           if (controlsShown) {
               focusCurrentChapter();
           } else {
               startChapterNotificationServiceIfNeeded();
           }
       }
       ```

4. Errors and fixes:
   - **Brace-less if/else inconsistency in `ScreensaverManager.java`**: The assistant mistakenly simplified `if (show) { ... } else { ... }` to a single-line brace-less form, which was inconsistent with project style. This was immediately self-detected and reverted back to the braced form. No user feedback was involved; the assistant caught and corrected this on its own.

5. Problem Solving:
   - The main challenge was identifying meaningful refactoring opportunities across a large Android TV codebase (~400 Java files) without changing behavior.
   - Key patterns found and addressed: backward-compatibility chains, duplicated method bodies, repeated conditional patterns, intermediate variables that could be eliminated, double-calls to the same method, and lambda verbosity.
   - The `fromString()` backward-compat chain was identified as the single biggest improvement in round 1 (50+ lines → ~8 lines).
   - The `VideoPlayerGlue` button-registration pattern was the biggest improvement in round 2 (~55 3-line if-blocks → helper method + single-line calls).

6. All user messages:
   - "Please review the current codebase and perform a general refactoring to improve its overall structure and quality."
   - "Please continue with another round of general refactoring to further improve the codebase."
   - "CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools. [...]" (this is the summary request)

7. Pending Tasks:
